  "brief": "EQT to acquire Range Resources in an all-stock deal worth $13 billion, creating a top US gas producer.\n\nEQT / Range Resources (Announced): EQT to Acquire Range Resources. EQT agrees to acquire Range Resources in an all-stock deal [1, 8]. The deal is expected to create a top US gas producer [2, 5]. The acquisition is part of an all-stock deal worth $13 billion [2, 3, 5]. The deal was announced on October 26 [1, 7, 8].\nRight Lane Industries / Capacity Trucks and LayMor (Announced): Right Lane Industries Acquires Capacity Trucks and LayMor. Right Lane Industries has acquired Capacity Trucks and LayMor from Terex [9, 10]. The deal was completed after a short period of time [10]. No further information is available [10].\nHealthSpan Partners / Surgery Partners (Announced): HealthSpan Partners Acquires Surgery Partners. HealthSpan Partners is acquiring Surgery Partners in a $5.7 billion deal [11, 12]. The deal will take Surgery Partners private [11, 12]. Bain Capital will remain involved with the company [12].\nOvintiv / Logan Energy (Announced): Ovintiv to Acquire Logan Energy. Ovintiv is acquiring Logan Energy for $890M [13, 14]. The deal will be structured in cash and shares [14]. Logan Oil Corp will be spun out [14].\nAcuity Inc. / Parameter Technologies (Announced): Acuity Inc. to Acquire Parameter Technologies. Acuity Inc. is acquiring Parameter Technologies [16, 15]. The deal was announced by Acuity and Parameter [16, 15]. The acquisition is part of Distech Controls [15].\ni-Tail / Phelps Pet Products (Completed): i-Tail Acquires Phelps Pet Products. i-Tail has completed its acquisition of Phelps Pet Products [17]. The deal was valued at $160 million [17]. The acquisition is now complete [17].\nUFP Industries / Apache Products (Announced): UFP Industries Acquires Apache Products. UFP Industries is acquiring Apache Products [18]. The deal is expanding UFP Industries' pallet manufacturing network [18]. No further information is available [18].\nOnsemi / Codasip (Announced): Onsemi Acquires Codasip. Onsemi has acquired Codasip's low-end RISC-V business [19, 20]. The deal is valued at $14.5 million [19]. Synaptics shares surged 14% on the merger announcement with Onsemi [20]. Cirrus Logic is expected to bid for Synaptics after the Onsemi deal [21].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- ClearOne's Oct. 14 Filing Disclosed a $200,000 Working-Capital Loan [22].\n- IT Services M&A Slows, But Buyers Remain Hungry For MSPs And AI Solutions [23].\n- Currier Plastics rebrands as Alentra following acquisitions [24].",
